I walk to the next stall.
A woman is selling ceramics here.
I see many plates and cups.
The things are all handmade.
I see a blue cup.
The cup is really very beautiful.
I pick it up.
The seller smiles at me.
I ask: “Excuse me, how much is this?”
The seller says: “That comes to thirty-five euros.”
Thirty-five euros?
That is unfortunately too expensive for me.
I am not buying the cup today.
I say: “Oh, unfortunately that is too expensive.”
I put the cup back on the table.
I smile and say: “Thank you anyway.”
The woman says in a friendly way: “No problem.”
“Have a nice day!”
I answer: “Thanks, you too!”
I say goodbye and walk on.
